      "notes": "The Living Lands is a text-based fantasy RPG. All content is conveyed through written descriptions and status readouts, not visual depictions, so there are no graphic images of any kind.\r\n\r\nViolence: Combat is central to the game. Fights are described in text, with references to weapons, wounds, blood, and death. Enemies and characters can be killed, and defeated foes leave corpses that can be looted. The tone is that of classic fantasy adventure, comparable to a tabletop RPG or a fantasy novel. The violence is stylized and not gratuitous, but it is persistent and frequent.\r\n\r\nDark fantasy themes: The world includes undead, necromancy (raising and commanding the dead), monsters, and a story that touches on death and mortality. Some zones and enemies carry a grim or unsettling tone.\r\n\r\nAlcohol: The game world includes taverns and drinkable beverages, including alcohol, as part of its fantasy setting.\r\n\r\nNo sexual content: The game contains no depictions of sexual acts, sexual assault, or nudity.\r\n\r\nThere is no depiction of real-world drug abuse, self-harm, or sexual violence."
